VALUES ('OTIS','bull_case','editorial_analysis','OTIS WORLDWIDE CORP''s position in elevators, escalators, installation, modernization, maintenance contracts, digital monitoring, and building-mobility services can compound value if demand converts into durable share, pricing, and cash rather than temporary volume. Engineering qualifications, distribution, installed equipment, regulatory approvals, customer integration, and service capability can create durable positions. Operating leverage and disciplined reinvestment can expand per-share free cash flow when revenue quality, margins, and capital intensity improve together. Official filings and earnings materials create a quarterly scorecard for testing management''s claims against delivered results and cash conversion.','Preserves the constructive interpretation as a sourced, reviewable claim.','OTIS official investor materials','https://www.otisinvestors.com/','Use the company''s official results, presentations, webcast replays, prepared remarks, and transcripts when the issuer makes them publicly available.','2026-08-02','published','Founding editorial research',CURRENT_TIMESTAMP,CURRENT_TIMESTAMP)
